  "question": {
    "text": "The potential energy for a force field $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}$ is given by $U(x, y)=\\cos (x+y)$. The force acting on a particle at position given by coordinates $(0, \\pi / 4)$ is $-$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FGSFO",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{j}})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECWb7",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\hat{i}+\\hat{j})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "P8ndH",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "i5PX1",
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{x}}=-\\frac{\\partial \\mathrm{U}}{\\partial \\mathrm{x}}=\\sin (\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y})$\n$$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{y}}=-\\frac{\\partial \\mathrm{U}}{\\partial \\mathrm{x}}=\\sin (\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}) \\\\\n\\left.\\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{x}}=\\sin (\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y})\\right]_{(0, \\pi / 4)}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\n\\left.\\mathrm{~F}_{\\mathrm{y}}=\\sin (\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y})\\right]_{(0, \\pi / 4)}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\n\\therefore \\mathrm{F}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{j}}]\n\\end{array}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
